    "id": "wcabuneon_1",
    "stac_version": "1.1.0",
    "description": "This dataset provides individual-crown polygons and associated live woody aboveground biomass (AGB) estimates for 15 National Ecological Observatory Network (NEON) sites across the western United States. The dataset includes approximately 46.4 million mapped crowns distributed across the ABBY, CLBJ, JORN, KONZ, MOAB, NIWO, NOGP, ONAQ, RMNP, SJER, SOAP, SRER, TEAK, WREF, and YELL sites. The study areas range from approximately 100 to 368 km\u00b2 per site and span a broad environmental gradient, including humid temperate and montane forests, open woodlands, grasslands, and arid and semiarid shrublands. The data corresponds to site-specific NEON airborne acquisition years from 2020 to 2023. Because the data are provided as vector crown delineations in shapefiles, their fundamental spatial unit is the individual woody crown rather than a fixed raster pixel; the source spectral products used in crown characterization had a spatial resolution of 1 m. This dataset is a Level 4 derived data product generated from NEON Airborne Observation Platform LiDAR, hyperspectral, and high-resolution RGB imagery, supplemented with NEON vegetation surveys, Forest Inventory and Analysis data, and published allometric equations. The data are provided in shapefile and comma-separated values format.",
